    "description": "Picatinny AR Grip Mount: Laffs Dynamics\n\nA picatinny mount, adapts AR-15 grips for the use as dedicated angled or vertical foregrips. \n\nAny AR-15 grip with an angle of less or more than 90° is considered an angled foregrip if used in conjunction with \nthe Picatinny AR Grip Mount. An AR-15 grip with an angle of EXACTLY 90° will be considered a vertical foregrip if \nused with the Picatinny AR Grip Mount. \n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 220C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .20mm \nStandard Layer Height: .16mm\nWall Thickness: .40 \nWall Perimeters: 5+\nInfill: 32%\nInfill Pattern: Gyroid\nSupport Material Percentage: 18% \n\n\n\nHardware Needed:\n\n1x Allen Head Screw, 1/4-28 x 1\"\n\n1x Steel Star Washer\n\n1x M4x30mm Bolt (Can be ground down to 28mm so it doesn't stick out the side)\n\n1x M4 Hex Nut",
